    {
      "id": "claim_f2e5faa6146c4b61b9f672b1e124bf9d",
      "statement": "At startup, applyStagedRestore runs as the first step of initializeDatabase (before the database handle is opened): it validates the restore-pending.json marker (rejecting missing paths, NUL bytes, and any staged or target path containing '..' or backslash), verifies the staged file exists, atomically renameSyncs it over the target DB, deletes the marker, and after schema/migrations records a backup.restore_completed audit event; on any failure the marker is renamed to restore-pending.json.failed and the current database is kept, leaving the server bootable.",
