    {
      "id": "claim_aa1f762ad84440cea9c6e447ddc8f86e",
      "statement": "RetentionService is the scheduled purge counterpart to backups: gated by RETENTION_ENABLED (default true), it purges rows older than RETENTION_DAYS (default 90) from experience_embeddings, trajectory_steps, vector_memories (only rows with ttl IS NULL), cognitive_episodes, and cognitive_patterns, while llm_provider_metrics, model_routing_decisions, and model_execution_outcomes use a fixed 30-day cutoff; start() runs a purge at boot when RETENTION_RUN_ON_STARTUP is not 'false' and recurs every RETENTION_INTERVAL_HOURS (default 24). Per OBS-003 each table outcome is explicit: only a 'no such table' failure is the known no-op ('missing', 0 deletions), other errors record status 'error' with deleted null; every tick reports via noteScheduler/markRun so a failing purge marks the 'retention' scheduler 'failing' in the cockpit scheduler registry.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/server/src/__tests__/retention-errors.test.ts#L13-L61",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:422167d5faf89521e45af164f045259c8af4db121753d162f1686752512811a1:"
        },
