    {
      "id": "claim_c56e8433ad0148aea8babc705c957d55",
      "statement": "DiskGuardService is read-only capacity alerting created after a 2026-09-21 incident where a full disk crashed SQLite with SQLITE_IOERR_SHMSIZE: default off (DISK_GUARD_ENABLED=true to enable), it statfs's DISK_GUARD_PATH (default /data) every 10 minutes (first check 30s after start, unref'd timer), classifies levels at DISK_GUARD_WARN_PCT (default 80) and DISK_GUARD_CRITICAL_PCT (default 90), and on warn/critical upserts one work item per day and level (source disk_guard, source_ref '<day>:<level>') plus one djimitflo.alert.disk outbox event per new item, never deleting anything.",
